 "notes": "Headline observed 95% C.L. limit on the ALP-neutron coupling, Fig.3 (PlotA.pdf), traced as the lower boundary of the combined blue \"This work\" excluded region (union of datasets I [Vasilakis], II [Kornack], III [Brown]). Paper defines the coupling via L = -g_aNN (d_mu a) Nbar gamma5 gamma^mu N (Eq.5), i.e. g_aNN in GeV^-1 with the single-derivative (non-2m_N) normalisation. Converted to the canonical dimensionless g_an using the 2m_N rule: g_an = 2 m_n g_aNN with m_n = 0.9396 GeV (factor 1.879). Native g_aNN ranges ~2.2e-7 (flat, low mass) down to a minimum ~3.3e-10 near m_a~1.5e-14 eV, rising to ~4e-9 near 5e-13 eV. Dataset III provides the flat/low-mass bound extending to arbitrarily small mass; a modest bump near 2-4e-17 eV is the weakly-covered transition between dataset III (ends ~3e-18 eV) and dataset I (starts 2.4e-17 eV). Right edge ~5e-13 eV (dataset II upper reach 4e-13 eV; points beyond trimmed). DM density assumed rho_a=rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (not rescaled). Extracted by pixel-tracing a raster render of the vector figure; axis calibrated from vector text tick positions.",
